  "content": {
    "id": "p19-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Find the inverse function of:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p19-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=2x+5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x-5}{2}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=2x+5\\\\x&=2y+5\\\\2y&=x-5\\\\y&=\\frac{x-5}{2}\\\\f^{-1}(x)&=\\frac{x-5}{2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=4-3x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{4-x}{3}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=4-3x\\\\x&=4-3y\\\\3y&=4-x\\\\y&=\\frac{4-x}{3}\\\\f^{-1}(x)&=\\frac{4-x}{3}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q9-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=x^3-2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f^{-1}(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x+2}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=x^3-2\\\\x&=y^3-2\\\\y^3&=x+2\\\\y&=\\sqrt[3]{x+2}\\\\f^{-1}(x)&=\\sqrt[3]{x+2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q9-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\frac{1}{x-5}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1}{x}+5$, $x\\ne0$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{1}{x-5}\\\\x&=\\frac{1}{y-5}\\\\x(y-5)&=1\\\\y-5&=\\frac{1}{x}\\\\y&=\\frac{1}{x}+5\\\\f^{-1}(x)&=\\frac{1}{x}+5\\end{align*}$$\nThe original domain excludes $5$ and its range excludes $0$. Hence the inverse has domain $\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{0\\}$ and range $\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{5\\}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q9-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\frac{x+1}{6}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f^{-1}(x)=6x-1$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{x+1}{6}\\\\x&=\\frac{y+1}{6}\\\\6x&=y+1\\\\y&=6x-1\\\\f^{-1}(x)&=6x-1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q9-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=12-3x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f^{-1}(x)=4-\\frac{x}{3}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=12-3x\\\\x&=12-3y\\\\3y&=12-x\\\\y&=4-\\frac{x}{3}\\\\f^{-1}(x)&=4-\\frac{x}{3}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q9-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\frac{4}{x+2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{4-2x}{x}$, $x\\ne0$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{4}{x+2}\\\\x&=\\frac{4}{y+2}\\\\x(y+2)&=4\\\\y+2&=\\frac{4}{x}\\\\y&=\\frac{4}{x}-2\\\\f^{-1}(x)&=\\frac{4-2x}{x}\\end{align*}$$\nThe original domain excludes $-2$ and its range excludes $0$. Hence the inverse has domain $\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{0\\}$ and range $\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{-2\\}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q9-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\frac{5}{x+3}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{5}{x}-3$, $x\\ne0$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{5}{x+3}\\\\x&=\\frac{5}{y+3}\\\\x(y+3)&=5\\\\y+3&=\\frac{5}{x}\\\\y&=\\frac{5}{x}-3\\\\f^{-1}(x)&=\\frac{5}{x}-3\\end{align*}$$\nThe original domain excludes $-3$ and its range excludes $0$. Hence the inverse has domain $\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{0\\}$ and range $\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{-3\\}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      }
    ]
  },
